// Sigil-Logic/clafer#46: an if-then-else with a numeric branch yields a number
// even when the other branch is a set, so `sum (if c then 5 else N.dref)` is
// rejected instead of rendering an illegal Alloy join (HOARDE Codex, PR #48
// Cycle 2).
abstract N ->> integer
n1 : N = 5
n2 : N = 2
x -> integer
[ x = sum (if some n1 then 5 else N.dref) ]
